WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.251
Since January first, 2026, there are exactly two lawful ways to work
with a residential buyer in Texas.

00:00:06.251 --> 00:00:13.011
You have to know which one you are in before the appointment starts —
not afterwards, and not once somebody asks.

00:00:13.211 --> 00:00:15.789
One prospect, two postures.

00:00:15.989 --> 00:00:21.876
Either your broker represents the buyer, under a
written agreement that says so.

00:00:21.876 --> 00:00:28.283
Or your broker shows property without representing the buyer, under
section 1101.562.

00:00:28.283 --> 00:00:32.179
There is no third position and no working it out later.

00:00:32.179 --> 00:00:35.815
The choice is made before the showing, in writing.

00:00:35.815 --> 00:00:39.361
The notice states the rule in the consumer's own words.

00:00:39.361 --> 00:00:43.756
A license holder who performs brokerage activity for a prospective

00:00:43.756 --> 00:00:48.073
buyer of residential property must enter into a written agreement

00:00:48.073 --> 00:00:52.467
with the buyer before showing any residential property to the buyer

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:58.557
or if no residential property will be shown, before presenting an
offer on behalf of the buyer.

00:00:58.757 --> 00:01:00.953
Two moments, and only two.

00:01:01.153 --> 00:01:10.096
The form then points you to section 1101.563 for what that agreement
must contain, because the notice summarises and the statute defines.

00:01:10.096 --> 00:01:13.663
Now the other posture, and the form lists its conditions.

00:01:13.663 --> 00:01:20.649
The broker has not agreed with the buyer or tenant, either orally or
in writing, to represent the buyer or tenant.

00:01:20.649 --> 00:01:26.892
The broker is not otherwise acting as the buyer or tenant's agent at
the time of showing the property.

00:01:26.892 --> 00:01:34.992
The broker does not provide the buyer or tenant opinions or advice
regarding the property or real estate transactions generally.

00:01:34.992 --> 00:01:40.789
And the broker does not perform any other act of real estate
brokerage for the buyer or tenant.

00:01:40.989 --> 00:01:43.496
Four conditions, joined by and.

00:01:43.696 --> 00:01:47.189
Satisfy three and you are not inside this section at all.

00:01:47.189 --> 00:01:52.856
Read the paragraph underneath, because the
non-representation posture is papered too.

00:01:52.856 --> 00:01:57.466
Before showing a residential property to an unrepresented prospective

00:01:57.466 --> 00:02:01.547
buyer, a license holder must enter into a written agreement that

00:02:01.547 --> 00:02:07.064
contains the information required by section 1101.563 of the Texas
Occupations Code.

00:02:07.064 --> 00:02:11.901
The agreement may not be exclusive and must be
limited to no more than 14 days.

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:19.717
One more gate stands before any showing without representation, and
which side you are on decides it.

00:02:19.717 --> 00:02:28.730
Represent the owner, and you make the representation disclosure —
orally or in writing — under section 1101.558(b).

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:35.259
Represent nobody, and you deliver the written
notice under section 1101.558(b-1).

00:02:35.459 --> 00:02:37.246
That is the IABS.

00:02:37.446 --> 00:02:41.238
Here is where this fails, and it is never at the paperwork.

00:02:41.238 --> 00:02:47.241
It fails in a hallway, when someone you are not representing asks
whether the price is fair.

00:02:47.241 --> 00:02:51.506
Section 1101.562(c) lets you confirm the size, price and terms.

00:02:51.706 --> 00:02:53.786
Confirm — not evaluate.

00:02:53.986 --> 00:02:56.829
Have the sentence ready before you need it.

00:02:56.829 --> 00:03:03.227
I can't give you an opinion on that, because I'm showing you this
house without representing you.

00:03:03.427 --> 00:03:05.191
Then stop talking.
